+## Sales and variance
+
+- `POST /import/sales` takes `{ "csv": "..." }` with the columns
+  `ticket,soldAt,dishId,qty` (`soldAt` is an ISO instant, `qty` a whole
+  number). Each dish uses one portion of its recipe per `qty`; ingredients
+  are consumed at `soldAt` with the ledger `ref` `sale:<ticket>`. Tickets
+  already imported are skipped. Answers `{ "tickets": n, "dishes": n }`
+  (`dishes` is the total quantity sold). A bad row is `bad_request` and an
+  item running out is `sale_out_of_stock` (409); either way the message names
+  the row (`row 2` is the first data row) and nothing is imported.
+- `GET /reports/variance?from=YYYY-MM-DD&to=YYYY-MM-DD` lists, per item,
+  `theoretical` use from the sales sold in those days (inclusive), `actual`
+  use (every `consume` movement in those days) and `difference` (actual minus
+  theoretical), for items where either is above zero.
